WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.300
From action-packed, timey-wimey sci-fi adventures
to a surreal journey through the human mind,

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.260
these are the shows you should be watching
in 2018.

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:11.800
Throw some popcorn in the microwave and dig
out your binge-watching sweatpants, because

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:13.060
we're diving in.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.460
HBO's True Detective brought Cary Fukunaga's
work to a mainstream audience.

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:22.270
His keen eye for cinematography was a key
component of the show's season one success.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:26.689
After that, he released Beasts of No Nation,
which was met with similarly positive critical

00:00:26.689 --> 00:00:27.180
acclaim.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:31.220
Then, he more or less disappeared for three
years before blazing back to the small screen

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:31.940
with Maniac.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.160
The wait was worth it.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:38.120
Starring Jonah Hill and Emma Stone as patients
in an experimental mental health study in

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:43.290
a retro-futuristic dystopia, the beautifully
shot Maniac jumps from genre to genre through

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:44.940
Owen and Annie's fantasies.

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:49.840
And Fukunaga keeps the focus squarely on the
difficulty of living with mental illness and

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:54.559
trauma, and the possibility of finding connection
and community despite, or even because of,

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:55.200
those issues.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:57.580
"Of course you make me happy.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:02.680
You always made me happy."

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:08.340
Donald Glover and his team had a lot to live
up to when the second season of Atlanta was

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:12.409
announced, the show's first season firmly
established it as one of the most electrifying

00:01:12.409 --> 00:01:14.400
television series in recent memory.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:19.180
And Glover's performance as Earn in season
two of Atlanta, subtitled "Robbin' Season,"

00:01:19.189 --> 00:01:23.620
is as good as you'd expect, but it also showcases
the other characters with a confidence that

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:25.359
you won't see on any other show.

00:01:25.359 --> 00:01:29.569
The season was filled with standout episodes
highlighting the other characters in the show,

00:01:29.569 --> 00:01:34.109
like the nightmarish "Teddy Perkins," which
followed Darius, played by Lakeith Stanfield,

00:01:34.109 --> 00:01:37.200
meeting a Michael Jackson-esque musician in
an ominous mansion.

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:40.980
"Woods," on the other hand, followed Brian
Tyree Henry's Al, A.K.A.

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:45.960
"Paper Boi," as he's haunted by the downsides
of his own fame and success.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:47.640
"Keep standing still, you're gone, boy.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.259
You're wasting time.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:53.140
And the only people who got time are dead."

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:58.030
More than half of the season was directed
by Hiro Murai, Glover's longtime music video

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:02.849
director, and Murai's expert visual sense
and rich use of surrealism has made Atlanta

00:02:02.849 --> 00:02:04.520
one of the best-looking shows on television.

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:11.220
After returning to television for the first
time in twenty years in 2005, Doctor Who re-established

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:14.310
itself as a stylish sci-fi show for a new
audience.

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:19.020
Still, despite multiple showrunners and multiple
actors playing the eponymous Doctor, the next

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:24.040
decade of Doctor Who settled into a comfortable
rhythm: an eccentric male lead, on-again off-again

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:29.040
romances with various co-stars, callbacks
to the original run, and silly science-fiction

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.040
shenanigans.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:32.430
"Sko bo tro no fro jo."

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:35.740
"No bo ho sho ko ro to sho.

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:36.960
Forohopotokopojo."

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:44.180
That all changed in 2018 when, for the first
time, a woman took over as the title character.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.400
"What do we do?"

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:46.020
"Why are you asking her?"

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:47.220
"'Cause she's in charge, bro."

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:47.720
"Says who?"

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:49.060
"Says us!"

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:53.180
Jodie Whitaker's turn as the Doctor ended
up being exactly the shot in the arm that

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:56.960
the show needed, coinciding nicely with new
showrunner Chris Chibnall's tenure.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:02.580
The Haunting of Hill House is horror at its
best, simultaneously terrifying and thrilling

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:06.420
while also dealing with the emotional core
that should be at the center of every horror

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:06.920
movie.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:11.439
That richness of character has led to some
reviews calling Hill House "a drama with ghosts"

00:03:11.439 --> 00:03:15.550
or "like This Is Us wrapped in a gothic ghost
story," but make no mistake.

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:17.700
Hill House is absolutely terrifying.

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:30.180
Director/showrunner Mike Flanagan showcases
all the technical brilliance that made Oculus

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:34.379
and Gerald's Game so profoundly scary, and
through it all, he never loses sight of the

00:03:34.379 --> 00:03:38.610
fact that the ghosts are a way for the audience
to connect to the Crain family's trauma.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:41.520
It's just that, y'know, they're also scary
as hell.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:46.659
As the prequel, and sometimes-kinda-sequel
to Breaking Bad, Better Call Saul takes a

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:51.150
bit of a slower pace than its predecessor,
but is still prone to occasional explosions

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:51.800
of violence.

00:03:52.249 --> 00:03:56.359
You're more likely to see elaborate cons than
the vicious meth heads that populated Breaking

00:03:56.359 --> 00:04:01.049
Bad, but the underlying moral decay and fantastic
character writing is even better.

00:04:01.049 --> 00:04:05.230
Bob Odenkirk fills Jimmy with such warmth
and humanity that it's like watching a horror

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:08.180
movie as he slowly loses his last bits of
morality.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.760
"You think I'm some kind of lowlife, some
kind of ass----."

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:11.760
"What?"

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:12.980
"The kind of lawyer only guilty people hire,
right?"

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:13.980
"Jimmy, that's not…"

00:04:13.989 --> 00:04:15.840
"You look at me and you see 'Slippin' Jimmy.'"

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:20.459
Even for a show as consistent as Better Call
Saul, season four was a victory lap and took

00:04:20.459 --> 00:04:24.810
viewers closer to the events of Breaking Bad
than anyone really expected, and we couldn't

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:26.340
be more excited for what's to come.

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:31.300
We already know that Jimmy is destined for
moral rot and a job managing a Cinnabon, the

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:34.000
beauty of the show is how much you don't want
it to happen.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:39.500
DC's new take on a familiar cast of caped
crusaders, Titans needed just two glorious

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:41.449
words to get fans riled up:

00:04:41.449 --> 00:04:42.449
"F--- Batman."

00:04:42.449 --> 00:04:46.520
Sure, Robin and the rest of the titular team
look like they just bought out a Hot Topic,

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:49.800
but critics dig DC's gritty reimagining of
the young super heroes.

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:54.380
For instance, Autumn Noel Kelly at Newsweek
wrote positively about the show, claiming:

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:57.100
"Titans is the most balanced superhero show
out there.

00:04:57.370 --> 00:05:01.200
It's skillfully constructed, narratively speaking,
and there's a surprising amount of flavor

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.400
beneath its classification as a dark, moody,
teen drama."

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:06.620
But really, you know why you're watching.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.040
"F--- Batman."

